{"abstract":"Disclosure of data analytics results has important scientific and commercial justifications. However, no data shall be disclosed without a diligent investigation of risks for privacy of subjects. Privug is a tool-supported method to explore information leakage properties of data analytics and anonymization programs. In Privug, we reinterpret a program probabilistically, using off-the-shelf tools for Bayesian inference to perform information-theoretic analysis of the information flow. For privacy researchers, Privug provides a fast, lightweight way to experiment with privacy protection measures and mechanisms. We show that Privug is accurate, scalable, and applicable to a range of leakage analysis scenarios.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Pardo, Raúl","Rafnsson, Willard","Probst, Christian","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695269"],"event":{"acronym":"ESORICS","end":"2021-10-08","place":"VIRTUAL","start":"2021-10-04","title":"European Symposium on Research in Computer Security","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["New Zealand"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","UNITEC Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Anonymization Programs","Bayesian inference","Data analytics","Information leakage","Privacy Protection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"privug using probabilistic programming for quantifying leakage in privacy risk analysis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/93413939/21_esorics_privug.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-695269","identifier":[{"id":"85117143748","type":"scopus"}],"ids"